# Supabase migrations

When you add or modify SQL under `supabase/migrations/` (or the user asks to apply a migration), **apply it to the project database** — do not only tell the user to paste into the SQL Editor.

Use the repo script (requires `secrets/supabase.env` with `SUPABASE_DB_URL` or `DATABASE_URL`):

```powershell
cd C:\Projects\Afterten
node scripts/supabase/apply-sql-file.mjs supabase/migrations/<filename>.sql
```

Apply migrations in timestamp order if several are new and depend on each other. After applying, optionally verify with:

```powershell
node scripts/supabase/query.mjs "select ..."
```

If `secrets/supabase.env` is missing, say so and point to `secrets/supabase.env.example` — do not commit secrets.
